          <td>The name said logging; the worker created inventory units. Nobody could reason about the fleet from its own names.</td>
          <td>Old queue drained to zero before the cutover, so no job was stranded under the dead name.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Two new certificate queues<br><span class="tk">Aug 2026</span></td>
          <td>Bid-certificate and order-result jobs were sharing one general-purpose queue with everything else in that integration.</td>
          <td>5 replicas each on two machines — the change that takes the fleet to <strong>142</strong> in development, where it ships first. Production, sandbox and pre-production stay at 122 until it rolls out there.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Order initiation pinned at <strong>1</strong><br><span class="tk">standing rule</span></td>
